TRAFFIC METHOD
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  flows.py (evidence/28863/tools): four raw AF_PACKET flows, 500 pps each, ethertype
  0x88B5, payload = tag + seq + send epoch; receivers on eth2 and eth3 record every
  frame with its receive epoch (sudo, tb470 /tmp/ck15 only):
    B32 broadcast eth3->eth2   B23 broadcast eth2->eth3
    U32 unicast eth3->eth2 MAC U23 unicast eth2->eth3 MAC
  flowstat.py counts lost / duplicate seqs and each run of missing seqs (2 ms per
  frame). "Echo" = a NIC receiving frames of the flow it SENDS (only a loop can return
  a broadcast to the port it came in on).
  Failover trigger: reload.py sends `reload stack-member N`, waits for "(y/n)", sends
  "y"+CR and stamps that epoch (= t0), then records the reloading member's console.
  Pollers every 3 s: `show clock`/`show stack`/`show mrp ring` on a stack console,
  `show mrp ring` on the SA. Each run lasts 360 s, with the reload at +~32 s.
  Clock alignment: device UTC = tb470 + 41-42 s (show clock vs epoch stamp, each run).

