READING
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  - The loop matches mrpd's own log line for line: at the master change (and at a
    member's late join), the MRM's test-frame monitoring expires
    (TestTimerExpired) although no ring link failed. mrpd sets the secondary
    port4.0.26 Forwarding and declares "Ring opened" on a closed ring. Its own test
    frames then come back and it re-blocks ("Ring closed"). The cycle repeats several
    times per event, with an FDB flush each time.
  - The false open is harmful only when the secondary port stays UP. Run B, whose
    failing master took the secondary port with it, had a clean master change. Runs
    A and C, where the ring stayed physically closed, looped.
  - `show mrp ring` does not show any of it: Network Status Closed, Topology Change
    Count 3 and MRC Link Change Count 4 in every 3 s sample of every run. Only the
    traffic and the syslog show it.
  - Not isolated (would need more runs): whether profile 500 (the longer test
    monitoring) avoids the false expiry, and whether the member-join trigger depends on
    which member joins. With 200 ms profile timers (20 ms x 3 = 60 ms monitoring) the
    master change evidently exceeds the window.

